        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY\r\nEXCELLENT 4 BEDROOM SEMI DETACHED RESIDENCE IN HIGHLY SOUGHT AFTER RESIDENTIAL LOCATION IN ATHENRY TOWN WITHIN SHORT WALK TO TRAIN STATION , TOWN CENTRE AND ALL THE FANTASTIC AMENITIES TO HAND\r\n\r\n30 CLUAIN LARA,\r\nRAHEEN ,\r\nATHENRY,\r\nCO. GALWAY\r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\nThe property is located in a lovely private cul de sac position within the well established Cluain Lara estate with large open estate green area to the front side and within a short stroll of Athenry town centre ,Athenry train station, various schools and amenities etc. EIRCODE : H65TC90\r\nCluain Lara is regarded as one of Athenry’s foremost and sought after residential estates offering an excellent location and quality of construction in a low density environment within the town .\r\n\r\nThis excellently located 4 bedroom property is located within walking distance of the Medieval and Heritage town centre of Athenry and is situated near Raheen community pitches.\r\n\r\nAthenry also benefits from it’s local railway station on the Galway / Dublin and Galway / Limerick lines with enhanced commuter rail service together with excellent access onto the nearby M6 Galway/Dublin motorway and the M17 Galway/Sligo route just outside Athenry providing for such a convenient and easily accessible residential destination only 20 minutes to Galway city\r\n\r\n\r\nGreat opportunity to acquire a fantastic spacious solid home in this prestigious development in a prime location within a short leisurely stroll to the towncentre,, local Athenry shopping centre, hotels and many excellent retail and residential amenities and facilities that the attractive Heritage and Medieval has to offer. The area boasts an excellent array of national and secondary schools all close by .\r\n\r\nAthenry is a progressive and superbly located town that is experiencing enormous growth and prosperity and with the recent opening of the DEXCOM site which will provide approximately 1,000 jobs . Superb residential destination for a wide spectrum of discerning purchasers.\r\nEIRCODE : H65TC90\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nThe property is a fine spacious 4 bedroom semi - detached house with a part red brick façade and nestling on a private cul-de-sac end site within the Cluain Lara Estate within walking distance of Athenry town centre, train station and all the wide array of amenities and facilities available in this attractive characteristic Medieval and historic Market town . The property has a spacious and bright interior with a beautiful sitting room with feature fireplace, a fine kitchen / dining area with fitted kitchen units with electric oven and hob ,tiled flooring and spacious utility with back door. A nice entrance hall with downstairs toilet completes the ground floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nUpstairs there are 4 bedrooms with master en-suite and main bathroom. The property has a low maintenance exterior with part red brick, part render front façade together with pebble dash finish to side and rear.\r\n\r\nOutside, the property has a small front garden area and tarmac drive parking area together with rear paved patio and good size rear enclosed garden area with a south facing aspect. There is an outside boiler room and small timber garden shed. The property has oil fired central heating and PVC double glazed windows.\r\n\r\nThe property has a Gross Internal Floor Area of approx. 1,162 sq ft/ 108 sq m plus front porch canopy and rear integral boiler house.\r\n\r\nBER Rating ; “C”\r\n\r\nBER NO : 119516615\r\n\r\nCOMMENT ::\r\nExcellent opportunity to acquire a fine 4 bedroom house in a lovely\r\nprivate position within one of Athenry’s most popular well established\r\nestates with a large centre green area and within a short stroll to the towncentre.\r\n\r\nGUIDE PRICE: €395,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ACCOMMODATION: Approx Dimensions ( M )\r\n\r\nGround Floor :\r\n\r\nFront open Porch\r\nEntrance hall c. 4.618 X 1.857 M. with tiled floor ,coving , stairway with carpet and understairs toilet.\r\nDownstairs Toilet with wc , whb , tiled.floor\r\n\r\nSitting room c. 5.442 x 3.596 M with solid timber floor , feature cast iron fireplace and timber surround ,coving, and nice small front bay window area .\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen / dining room c. 5.556 x 3.967 M with tiled floor, original fitted kitchen with electric oven and hob ,, ssu and plumbed for dishwasher, double patio doors to rear patio and garden area\r\n\r\nUtility c. 2.426 x 1.77 M with tiled floor and generous worktop and counter area plumbed for washing machine and dryer, back door .\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst floor / Upstairs\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 / Master Bedroom -(Front)\r\nc. 3.977 x 3.355 M - including en-suite\r\nbedroom with carpet , BIW , plus small bay window area.\r\n\r\nEn-suite with wc, whb, shower unit off mains, tiled walls and floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (Front) c. 2.115 x 1.573 M PLUS 1.464 X 1.034 M with carpet , - ideal home office / study room etc\r\nLanding : spacious landing with carpet , hot press with shelving, access to attic.\r\n\r\nMain bathroom c. 1.982 x 1.927 M with wc, whb, bath and shower , fully tiled throughout\r\nBedroom 3 c. 3.351 x 3.054 M with BIW , carpet – lovely bright room at back\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 c. 2.984 X 2.392 M with BIW ,carpet.\r\n\r\n\r\nOutside:\r\nTarmac drive forecourt with ample car parking\r\nSmall front verge garden with good side pedestrian access way to rear garden\r\nand high estate block wall on the flat\r\nSpacious enclosed rear garden with nice lawn and patio area with doors to\r\nkitchen/dining area.\r\nIntegral Boiler house approx. 1.972 x 1.023 M with power supply\r\nSmall timber garden shed\r\nNice Side pedestrian passage – c. 1.397 M average width and flanked by high estate wall on the flat."
